+/*
+ * (xnu 0187) Re-vote the GPU's speed after boot: the same HFI_GX_BW_PERF_VOTE message step 17 sends
+ * once (a different table index; the GMU already has the whole table from step 16's HFI_PERF_TABLE,
+ * so nothing is reloaded). For sweet_cpufreq.c's thermal governor, which until now read the GPU's own
+ * TSENS sensor (TSENS_GPU) only to print it: the GPU ran at whatever sweetgpulevel asked for at boot,
+ * unmanaged, for as long as the phone has been kept on and drawing through Turnip/Metal.
+ * level 0 ("off") is refused: this only ever lowers or restores, never powers the core down.
+ * false: not kept on yet, a bad level, or the GMU refused/did not answer (kept.khz is unchanged
